1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,933
Marco 的分支是一次很大的提交（commit）
Marco's branch arrived as one large commit:

2
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:07,317
213 个文件，新增约 46,000 行
213 files and about 46,000 new lines.

3
00:00:07,637 --> 00:00:09,621
这些行大多不是代码
Most of those lines are not code.

4
00:00:09,941 --> 00:00:14,080
它们是证据：测试问题、保存下来的检索结果，以及打分
They are evidence: test questions, saved search results, and grades.

5
00:00:14,317 --> 00:00:16,661
几乎所有内容都围绕一个问题
Almost all of it is about one question:

6
00:00:16,661 --> 00:00:21,229
来电者问了一个问题，检索能不能把对的段落交给 agent？
when a caller asks something, does search hand the agent the right passages?

7
00:00:21,549 --> 00:00:23,256
Marco 调了三个旋钮
Marco turned three dials.

8
00:00:23,576 --> 00:00:25,176
文档怎么切
How the documents are cut.

9
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:27,010
检索怎么跑
How the search is run.

10
00:00:27,096 --> 00:00:28,738
结果怎么排序
And how results are ordered.

11
00:00:29,058 --> 00:00:31,725
他还加了一个检查口头回答的方法
He also added a way to check the spoken answers.

12
00:00:32,767 --> 00:00:34,580
先说：怎么给一次检索打分？
First, how do you score a search?

13
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:40,602
提一个问题，取它返回的前 5 段，由人逐段打分
You ask a question, take the top 5 passages it returns, and a person grades each one:

14
00:00:40,602 --> 00:00:45,567
没帮助给 0，部分有帮助给 1，能回答问题给 2
0 if it does not help, 1 if it partly helps, 2 if it answers the question.

15
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:49,186
Precision@5（前 5 精确率）是这 5 段里有帮助的比例
Precision at 5 is the share of the five that help at all,

16
00:00:49,186 --> 00:00:50,699
这里是 5 段中 2 段
here 2 out of 5.

17
00:00:50,749 --> 00:00:53,849
MRR 只看第一段有帮助的段落
MRR looks only at the first helpful passage:

18
00:00:53,849 --> 00:00:56,808
它排在第 2 位，所以得分是二分之一
it is at rank 2, so the score is one half.

19
00:00:57,128 --> 00:00:58,728
排在第 1 位就得 1 分
Rank 1 would score 1.

20
00:00:58,817 --> 00:01:02,230
NDCG 奖励把最好的段落排在前面
NDCG rewards putting the best passages first.

21
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:08,204
它先给我们的排序打分，再给同一批段落的最佳排序打分，然后相除
It scores our order, then scores the best possible order of the same passages, and divides.

22
00:01:08,524 --> 00:01:10,124
1 表示排序完美
1 means perfect order.

23
00:01:10,284 --> 00:01:12,545
这三个数字都取决于人工打分
All three numbers depend on the grades.

24
00:01:12,865 --> 00:01:14,465
没有打分，就没有分数
No grades, no score.

25
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,161
第一个旋钮是切块（chunking）
The first dial is chunking.

26
00:01:17,413 --> 00:01:19,430
Marco 比较了三种切块器（chunker）
Marco compared three chunkers.

27
00:01:19,589 --> 00:01:21,935
A 是第 2 集里原来的那个
A is the original one from episode 2.

28
00:01:22,255 --> 00:01:25,003
B 从不把不同标题下的小节合在一起
B never merges sections with different headings,

29
00:01:25,003 --> 00:01:27,866
并且会重复表格里写着项目名称的那几行
and repeats the table rows that name the programs.

30
00:01:28,186 --> 00:01:30,554
C 切出用来检索的小段落
C makes small passages for searching,

31
00:01:30,554 --> 00:01:33,818
每段都连着一个更大的父段落（parent），用来补充上下文
each linked to a larger parent passage for context.

32
00:01:34,067 --> 00:01:37,264
为了公平比较，他另建了三个测试资料库
To compare them fairly, he built three separate test libraries,

33
00:01:37,264 --> 00:01:39,781
叫做 staging knowledge base（预发布知识库）
called staging knowledge bases,

34
00:01:39,781 --> 00:01:41,726
主资料库一点没动
and left the main one untouched.

35
00:01:42,046 --> 00:01:45,554
资料库 C 就是他的语音演示所指向的那个
Library C is the one his voice demo points at,

36
00:01:45,554 --> 00:01:47,613
也就是第 0 集里见过的那个 ID
the ID we met in episode 0.

37
00:01:47,850 --> 00:01:51,551
他向三个库问了同样的 25 个问题
He asked the same 25 questions to all three,

38
00:01:51,551 --> 00:01:56,767
每次取前 5 段，并且手工给全部 375 段打了分
took the top 5 each time, and graded all 375 passages by hand.

39
00:01:57,087 --> 00:01:59,537
团队文档说这些打分是暂定的（provisional）
The team's notes call these grades provisional.

40
00:02:00,517 --> 00:02:03,611
我们用 Marco 自己的评分脚本，在他的打分上重新算了一遍
We reran Marco's own scoring script on his grades.

41
00:02:03,909 --> 00:02:07,813
原来的切块器 A 精确率和 NDCG 最高
The original chunker A has the best precision and NDCG.

42
00:02:08,133 --> 00:02:12,848
分层切块器 C 能稍早一点找到第一段有帮助的段落
The hierarchical chunker C finds the first helpful passage a little sooner.

43
00:02:13,168 --> 00:02:14,768
B 在三项指标上都最低
B is lowest on all three.

44
00:02:15,066 --> 00:02:17,498
三者每次检索都大约要 0.4 秒
All three take about four tenths of a second.

45
00:02:17,734 --> 00:02:21,915
逐题来看，A 有 9 次最好，C 有 7 次
Question by question, A was best 9 times and C 7 times.

46
00:02:22,235 --> 00:02:25,329
6 题打平，B 从来没有单独拿过第一
6 were ties, and B was never best on its own.

47
00:02:25,649 --> 00:02:29,816
有 3 个问题，三个库都没找到任何有帮助的段落
For 3 questions, none of the three libraries found anything helpful,

48
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:32,881
尽管文档里确实出现了相关的词
although related words do appear in the documents.

49
00:02:33,201 --> 00:02:37,979
换一种切法没能解决它们，所以下一步该研究的就是这几个问题
Cutting the text differently did not fix them, so these are the questions to study next.

50
00:02:38,217 --> 00:02:41,993
这很重要，因为在这个分支上 B 成了默认切块器
That matters, because on this branch B becomes the default chunker.

51
00:02:42,313 --> 00:02:47,476
只有 25 个问题、打分又是暂定的，这些差距很小，可能会变
With 25 questions and provisional grades, these gaps are small and could change.

52
00:02:47,796 --> 00:02:49,854
但这里没有任何证据说明 B 更好
But nothing here shows B is better,

53
00:02:49,854 --> 00:02:54,089
在用它重建主资料库之前，值得先讨论一下
and that is worth discussing before the main library is rebuilt with it.

54
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:57,394
第二个旋钮是检索本身
The second dial is the search itself.

55
00:02:57,714 --> 00:03:01,917
在 feedback 模式下，retrieve 先用来电者的原话检索一次
In feedback mode, retrieve first searches with the caller's exact question.

56
00:03:02,237 --> 00:03:05,288
然后读一读返回的结果，可能再规划一次检索
Then it reads what came back, and may plan one more search.

57
00:03:05,608 --> 00:03:09,474
它执行这次检索，新段落只有和问题对得上才会留下
It runs it, keeps a new passage only if it matches the question,

58
00:03:09,474 --> 00:03:11,074
再把两份列表合并
and merges the two lists.

59
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:14,689
额外的检索词来自真实存在的文字
An extra search comes from words that are actually there:

60
00:03:14,689 --> 00:03:19,660
第一批结果里的某个标题或短语，并且和问题有共同的实词
a heading or phrase in the first results that shares real words with the question.

61
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:23,455
如果都不合格，就用来电者自己的关键词
If none qualifies, it uses the caller's own key words,

62
00:03:23,455 --> 00:03:25,214
再加一个来自固定小词表的变体
plus a variant from a short fixed list,

63
00:03:25,214 --> 00:03:27,830
比如 lonely（孤单）对应 companionship（陪伴）
like lonely to companionship.

64
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:30,448
对“我母亲洗澡需要帮忙”这个问题
For "my mother needs help showering",

65
00:03:30,448 --> 00:03:31,948
有一次运行加了检索词
one run added the search

66
00:03:31,948 --> 00:03:34,361
“bathing in bed, in the tub or shower”
"bathing in bed, in the tub or shower",

67
00:03:34,361 --> 00:03:36,534
这是个人护理（PCA）页面上的一句话
a line from the personal care page.

68
00:03:36,783 --> 00:03:38,867
这就是 model-free（不用模型）的意思
This is what model-free means:

69
00:03:38,867 --> 00:03:42,756
额外的检索词不是 AI 模型写的，只靠固定规则
no AI model writes the extra searches, only fixed rules.

70
00:03:43,076 --> 00:03:46,176
另一种模式叫 intent，会去问一个语言模型
Another mode, called intent, asks a language model,

71
00:03:46,176 --> 00:03:50,735
但 README 提醒，团队账号可能没有调用它的权限
but the README warns that the team's account may not be allowed to call it.

72
00:03:50,983 --> 00:03:55,455
合并列表时，每个段落在它出现的每份列表里都能得分
To merge the lists, each passage gets points from every list it appears in:

73
00:03:55,455 --> 00:03:59,687
排名越靠前分越高，第一次检索的分数乘以 1.5
more for a high rank, and the first search counts one and a half times.

74
00:04:00,007 --> 00:04:02,716
两次检索都找到的段落会往上升
A passage that both searches agree on rises.

75
00:04:03,036 --> 00:04:05,866
这叫做倒数排名融合（reciprocal rank fusion，RRF）
This is called reciprocal rank fusion.

76
00:04:05,916 --> 00:04:08,680
我们用 Marco 自己的合并代码验证了一个后果
We checked one consequence with Marco's own merge code.

77
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:14,056
只被额外检索找到的段落，最多得 61 分之 1
A passage found only by the extra search scores at most 1 over 61.

78
00:04:14,376 --> 00:04:19,283
第一次检索的第 10 名得 70 分之 1.5，比它更高
The tenth result of the first search scores 1.5 over 70, which is more.

79
00:04:19,603 --> 00:04:23,229
所以目前额外检索只能给第一次检索找到的结果重新排序
So today the extra search can reorder what the first search found.

80
00:04:23,549 --> 00:04:28,925
它无法把新段落加进前 5，除非第一次检索返回的结果不到 5 条
It cannot add a new passage to the top five, unless the first search returned fewer than five.

81
00:04:29,245 --> 00:04:32,949
代码注释看起来是希望新段落能进来的
The code's comments suggest new passages were meant to get in,

82
00:04:32,949 --> 00:04:35,518
所以这值得和 Marco 聊一聊
so this is worth a conversation with Marco.

83
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:38,288
Marco 保存了一次运行
Marco saved a run of 40 everyday home-care questions, with and without feedback.

84
00:04:38,288 --> 00:04:41,730
40 个日常居家护理问题，分别开、关 feedback
Marco saved a run of 40 everyday home-care questions, with and without feedback.

85
00:04:42,050 --> 00:04:44,674
其中 18 个问题用上了额外检索
Extra searches were used for 18 of them.

86
00:04:44,994 --> 00:04:49,772
40 个里有 23 个，前 5 段完全一样
For 23 of the 40, the top five passages came out exactly the same.

87
00:04:50,017 --> 00:04:51,617
feedback 要花时间
Feedback costs time.

88
00:04:51,809 --> 00:04:56,160
典型的一次检索从约 0.43 秒变成 0.51 秒
The typical search went from about 0.43 to 0.51 seconds,

89
00:04:56,160 --> 00:05:01,366
最慢的十分之一从约半秒变成约 1 秒
and the slowest tenth from about half a second to about one second.

90
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:06,955
关键的缺口在这里：那次运行里的 788 段，一段都没有打分
And here is the key gap: none of the 788 passages in that run were graded.

91
00:05:07,275 --> 00:05:09,997
所以它能告诉我们速度和行为
So the run tells us about speed and behaviour,

92
00:05:09,997 --> 00:05:12,779
却不能告诉我们 feedback 找到的段落是不是更好
but not whether feedback finds better passages.

93
00:05:13,017 --> 00:05:15,444
那次运行之后，规划器（planner）已经改过了
The planner has changed since that run.

94
00:05:15,494 --> 00:05:19,726
我们离线用今天的版本重放了同样 40 次第一次检索
We replayed today's version offline on the same 40 first searches:

95
00:05:19,726 --> 00:05:25,433
它给 17 个问题加了检索，几乎都是改写来电者自己的话
it adds a search for 17 questions, almost all of them rewrites of the caller's own words.

96
00:05:25,753 --> 00:05:28,612
而且 feedback 现在是语音应用的默认设置
And feedback is now the default in the voice app.

97
00:05:29,650 --> 00:05:32,466
最后一个旋钮检查的是回答，而不是段落
The last dial checks answers, not passages.

98
00:05:32,786 --> 00:05:35,026
一次测试通话会产生两份文字记录
A test call produces two transcripts.

99
00:05:35,346 --> 00:05:40,514
一个脚本把助手的回答和人写的参考答案作比较
A script compares the assistant's answer with a reference answer written by a person:

100
00:05:40,514 --> 00:05:43,250
共同的词、必须出现和禁止出现的说法
shared words, required and forbidden phrases,

101
00:05:43,250 --> 00:05:46,290
以及 agent 有没有真的去查
and whether the agent actually looked anything up.

102
00:05:46,533 --> 00:05:49,867
共同的词同样用余弦相似度（cosine similarity）来衡量
Shared words are measured with cosine similarity again,

103
00:05:49,867 --> 00:05:51,504
只是这次基于词频
this time over word counts.

104
00:05:51,824 --> 00:05:54,988
这里有个陷阱：一个美元金额写错的回答
That has a trap: an answer with one wrong dollar amount

105
00:05:54,988 --> 00:05:57,520
和正确答案几乎每个词都一样
shares almost every word with the right one.

106
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:01,594
Marco 的文档说得很直白：相似不等于正确
Marco's notes say it plainly: similarity is not correctness.

107
00:06:01,914 --> 00:06:04,176
事实仍然要由人来核对
A person still has to check the facts.

108
00:06:04,417 --> 00:06:07,830
目前只有一个参考答案，标注为入门示例（starter）
Right now there is one reference answer, marked as a starter.

109
00:06:08,150 --> 00:06:11,115
真正的测试需要 20 到 30 个核对过的参考答案
Real testing needs 20 to 30 checked ones.

110
00:06:12,150 --> 00:06:15,798
第 2 集结尾留下了一张藏起项目名称的表格
Episode 2 ended with a table that hid its program names.

111
00:06:16,118 --> 00:06:18,294
Marco 的分支从三处下手
Marco's branch attacks it three ways.

112
00:06:18,614 --> 00:06:20,337
新的切块器解决了它
The new chunker fixes it:

113
00:06:20,337 --> 00:06:23,990
我们验证过，写着 1,090 美元的那个 chunk 现在包含 JACC
we checked, and the 1,090 dollar chunk now says JACC.

114
00:06:24,310 --> 00:06:30,218
他为这份 PDF 写了一个新的提取器，但在真实文件上四页全部失败
A new extractor was written for that PDF, but on the real file it fails on all four pages,

115
00:06:30,218 --> 00:06:33,697
因为它找到 9 列，而它期望的是 7 列
because it finds nine columns where it expects seven.

116
00:06:34,017 --> 00:06:39,393
retrieve 现在会丢掉这张表里所有没被提取器验证过的 chunk
And retrieve now drops every chunk from that table that the extractor did not verify.

117
00:06:39,713 --> 00:06:42,827
所以目前这张表根本到不了 agent 手里
So for now, the table does not reach the agent at all.

118
00:06:43,067 --> 00:06:46,220
语音这边，电话号码要等 agent 复述
On the voice side, a phone number is saved only after the agent reads it back and the caller says yes.

119
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:49,232
一遍、来电者说“是”之后才会保存
On the voice side, a phone number is saved only after the agent reads it back and the caller says yes.

120
00:06:49,552 --> 00:06:53,563
而且空的检索结果不能再被当作证据
And empty search results can no longer be presented as evidence.

121
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,002
还没解决的：给 feedback 那次运行打分
What is open: grade the feedback run,

122
00:06:56,002 --> 00:06:59,453
最好在不知道哪段来自哪种模式的情况下打
ideally without knowing which mode produced which passage.

123
00:06:59,773 --> 00:07:02,504
决定合并时是否应该让新段落进来
Decide whether the merge should let new passages in.

124
00:07:02,824 --> 00:07:05,299
针对真实 PDF 修好提取器
Fix the extractor for the real PDF.

125
00:07:05,619 --> 00:07:10,760
决定哪个资料库上线，因为这些改动都还没进主资料库
Decide which library is the live one, since none of this is in the main library yet.

126
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:17,578
另外注意，这个分支把 AWS 账号和资料库 ID 放进了公开仓库
And note that the branch puts the AWS account number and library IDs into a public repository,

127
00:07:17,578 --> 00:07:19,997
而设置指南原本是把它们排除在外的
which the setup guide had kept out.

128
00:07:20,233 --> 00:07:22,089
三个问题，自我检测一下
Three questions to test yourself.

129
00:07:22,409 --> 00:07:26,441
为什么一次 MRR 满分的检索，精确率仍然可能很低？
Why can a search with a perfect MRR still have a low precision?

130
00:07:26,761 --> 00:07:30,836
为什么今天的额外检索能给前 5 重新排序，却加不进新段落？
Why can today's extra search reorder the top five but not add to it?

131
00:07:31,156 --> 00:07:35,081
为什么词的相似度高，并不能证明回答正确？
And why is high word similarity not proof of a correct answer?

132
00:07:35,317 --> 00:07:38,282
接下来，第 3 集深入一次检索的内部
Next, episode 3 goes inside a single search,

133
00:07:38,282 --> 00:07:42,527
第 4 集跟着一通完整的电话走一遍语音应用
and episode 4 follows a whole phone call through the voice app.
